                <pb facs="0746" n="646" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg646"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/6405: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Davis</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                            State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-02-20T17:00:00+00:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 20,
                                1920—5 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received February 20—3:06
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>291. With regard to the signing of the armistice between Latvia and the
                    Bolsheviks reported to have been signed yesterday I learn information at the
                    Foreign Office that Finland and Lithuania are expected to do likewise in the
                    immediate future.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Davis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
